 "note": "Busselton Pavilion (Parker Group gastropub, wine shop and distillery, opened 2024) at the north-east corner of Busselton Central, on Kent St. A skin over the base's generic shopping-centre box (its centroid is about 45 m away, so the box stays and this stands against its Kent St wall and in its alfresco notch). From the Landgate aerial (Oct 2026) and the venue's opening photo (Jan 2024): a square white vertical-board tower on the corner with BUSSELTON PAVILION in dark plain capitals over a black arched entry, the alfresco beside it (brick-red deck, market umbrellas, a black steel truss over it), a low white annex at the back of the alfresco, and the hall's white board front along Kent St. The arch is drawn square; colours of the umbrellas from the aerial. Plain lettering only. Metres: x left to right as seen from Kent St (east to west), y south from the box's Kent St wall.",
